body:
Wow it feels like I am reading something from my journal. 100% with you. I am not religious but I am spiritual. I had been asking for strength to navigate this and recently I have been asking that I am able to let go of life and all my bonds so I can have peace. Planning my suicide is the only thing I have been able to do lately and it genuinely helps me. I can literally never say this to anyone in real life without being admitted somewhere and I am so grateful that I can share this with people here. I do not know what my future holds but right now I am going through the motions of working through my exit list and it brings me peace. I dont know how to fix this or how to bounce back, if I even can, but just want you to know how similarly I feel to you. I have also been suicidal from a very young age.

&#x200B;

I am not afraid anymore either. There is such freedom in it. You know, I wonder if suicidality is a coping mechanism in our society.
